WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:02.909
- You don't know which
officer is going to show up.

00:00:02.909 --> 00:00:04.450
You don't know how they're going to react,

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:06.649
you don't know how the script works.

00:00:06.649 --> 00:00:09.140
The script is non-existent
for a lot of people

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:11.547
and that's where the problem is.

00:00:11.547 --> 00:00:14.179
It's a dice roll a lot of time.

00:00:14.179 --> 00:00:16.762
(solemn music)

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:21.368
It's just one of those
moments where like your

00:00:21.368 --> 00:00:23.119
mind just starts racing.

00:00:23.119 --> 00:00:26.117
How, like, what road is
this going to go down?

00:00:26.117 --> 00:00:28.259
I feel like at this point
you just, like, never know.

00:00:28.259 --> 00:00:29.958
- May parents, I forget
what they were doing,

00:00:29.958 --> 00:00:32.111
but I was standing outside.

00:00:32.111 --> 00:00:35.967
I was seven or eight and I
saw the police beat up a man.

00:00:35.967 --> 00:00:37.598
I remember not asking my parents about it

00:00:37.598 --> 00:00:39.716
because I had the very,
sort of, visceral sense

00:00:39.716 --> 00:00:42.549
that this is just how things were.

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:47.439
- I think of all the other people

00:00:47.439 --> 00:00:48.919
who were doing nothing wrong.

00:00:48.919 --> 00:00:51.419
And still died in a situation.

00:00:52.942 --> 00:00:54.999
It's just the fear of
knowing that I can do

00:00:54.999 --> 00:00:56.777
a million things that would seem harmless

00:00:56.777 --> 00:00:58.610
to me or anybody else.

00:00:59.457 --> 00:01:01.957
And that it could end my life.

00:01:04.437 --> 00:01:06.437
(sighs)

00:01:08.978 --> 00:01:10.548
- When you just look around a realize

00:01:10.548 --> 00:01:13.108
that the playing field is not level.

00:01:13.108 --> 00:01:15.528
- I definitely struggle
with whether it's even fair

00:01:15.528 --> 00:01:18.158
or ethical to bring a
black child into this world

00:01:18.158 --> 00:01:22.227
with things being the way that they are.

00:01:22.227 --> 00:01:24.680
- With the gamble to live in general,

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:27.586
but I think there's a
big difference between

00:01:27.586 --> 00:01:30.508
chance things that can
happen and then that there is

00:01:30.508 --> 00:01:34.348
people out here who
will target your child.

00:01:34.348 --> 00:01:36.249
- You know, they might be part of this

00:01:36.249 --> 00:01:40.658
ongoing theater of violence
without repercussion.

00:01:40.658 --> 00:01:41.938
I don't know if I have that in me.

00:01:41.938 --> 00:01:44.408
- I can't recall a certain
moment where I was like,

00:01:44.408 --> 00:01:47.769
"Oh, you know now this happened and so

00:01:47.769 --> 00:01:49.798
now as a result, like I'm scared."

00:01:49.798 --> 00:01:52.858
I think just probably
witnessing things over time.

00:01:52.858 --> 00:01:55.227
I don't think these are
necessarily new things,

00:01:55.227 --> 00:01:57.368
but with technology we just see them

00:01:57.368 --> 00:01:59.818
a lot more instantly.

00:01:59.818 --> 00:02:02.485
And it's definitely intensified.

00:02:06.792 --> 00:02:09.756
- I love to walk late at night,

00:02:09.756 --> 00:02:12.894
and while I think to think I present

00:02:12.894 --> 00:02:16.435
as pretty unassuming and non-threatening,

00:02:16.435 --> 00:02:18.745
there's always a chance that someone

00:02:18.745 --> 00:02:20.912
could not see me that way.

00:02:25.415 --> 00:02:29.582
- Stay safe but also, like,
don't let it change who you are.

00:02:30.515 --> 00:02:33.574
- I don't want them to
make us be afraid to love.

00:02:33.574 --> 00:02:35.324
And to have families.

00:02:36.265 --> 00:02:39.405
- All cops need to play by the same rules.

00:02:39.405 --> 00:02:41.655
And those rules need to be,

00:02:42.763 --> 00:02:44.897
that everyone is treated equally.

00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:48.314
That's what's at the core of all of this.

00:02:49.414 --> 00:02:51.997
(solemn music)

